<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trans-Iranian Railway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927–1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Trans-Iranian Railway is a railway built between 1927 and 1938 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Shah</a>, linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> by way of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>. Financed by taxes on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> rather than foreign loans, it crosses the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> mountains on hundreds of bridges and tunnels. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it carried Allied supplies to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>; it is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trans-iranian-railway.jpg" alt="Trans-Iranian Railway" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hhgygy · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Transiran_railway_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
